  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7232a3a6-7f13-5ed8-a851-294f1764af69" activityNameId="120758f8-8e97-5dbd-8555-eb0d4f50af3c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Nuclear fuel fabrication plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Nuclear fuel fabrication plant
Data on the construction of a UO2 fuel fabrication facility are pretty old and representing reference plants form US Studies on total material &amp; energy use in energy chains. It is roughly assumed that 100% of concrete with reinforcing bars are dumped in an depository for inerts. Only difference with equivalend dataset GLO is the use herewith of US electricity mix.;
UUID: 892e7951-5e81-3179-8192-963cff6a9ac5
The module includes: land use of the factory; energy (electricity and diesel) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled.
Location: North American and European conditions
Technology: Information regards facilities operating in the 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_892e7951-5e81-3179-8192-963cff6a9ac5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
